000200 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000300 PROGRAM-ID.   TDATECK2.
000400*REMARKS.
000500*    THIS IS A DATE UTILITY PROGRAM THAT WILL AID CALLING PROGRAMS
000600*    IN FORMATTING DATES IN EITHER AMERICAN OR EUROPEAN STYLE.
000700*
      *    HOW TO USE THIS SUBPROGRAM:
      *        IN MODE 0, FIRST DETERMINE THE DATE CODE (EITHER 1 OR 3)
001000*        THEN ADD 3 IF GOING BETWEEN DISPLAY AND DATABASE DATES,
001100*        ADD 6 IF BETWEEN SYSTEM AND DATABASE DATES, OR LEAVE ALONE
001200*        IF GOING BETWEEN SYSTEM AND DISPLAY DATES.  THEN THE
001300*        SUBPROGRAM WILL SIMPLY FLIP MONTH AND DAY IF ITS A
001400*        EUROPEAN PLANT AND IF YOU ADDED 0 OR 3 TO THE DATE CODE.
001500*
001600*        MODE 1 IS USED TO OBTAIN THE CURRENT DATE AND TIME IN THE
001700*        CORRECT STYLE FOR OUTPUT ON DOCUMENTS, SCREENS, REPORTS,
      *        AND FOR UPDATING THE DATABASE.  (DATABASE FORMAT IS THE
      *        SAME - YYMMDD - FOR EUROPEAN OR AMERICAN PLANTS).
002000*        IN MODE 1, JUST CALL THE PROGRAM AND THE CURRENT DATE
002100*        AND TIME WILL BE RETURNED IN VARIOUS FORMATS.  THEN
      *        USE THE FORMAT YOU NEED.  IF ITS A EUROPEAN PLANT,
      *        THE FORMATTED DATES WILL REFLECT THIS.
002400*
002500*        MODE 2 IS USED TO CONVERT A GIVEN SYSTEM DATE INTO
002600*        VARIOUS FORMATS IN THE CORRECT STYLE.
      *        IN MODE 2, PASS THE SYSTEM DATE ("CURRENT DATE")
002800*        IT WILL BE CONVERTED TO VARIOUS FORMATS IN THE
002900*        CORRECT DATE STYLE (AMERICAN OR EUROPEAN).  THEN
003000*        USE THE FORMAT YOU NEED.
003100*
003200*        MODE 3 IS USED TO VALIDATE A DATE INPUTTED FROM A SCREEN,
      *        AND CONVERT IT TO DATABASE FORMAT
003400*        IN MODE 3, PASS A DISPLAY DATE INPUTTED FROM A SCREEN.
003500*        IN A EUROPEAN PLANT, THE USER WILL INPUT THE DATE AS
003600*        DAY, THEN MONTH, THEN YEAR.  IN AN AMERICAN PLANT, THE
003700*        USER WILL INPUT THE DATE AS MONTH, THEN DAY, THEN YEAR.
003800*        THE DATE CAN BE PASSED IN ANY FORMAT (IE. FOR AMERICAN,
003900*        THE DATE COULD BE 3/23/85 OR MARCH 3 85 OR MAR 23/85,
004000*        ETC).  THIS DATE WILL THEN BE VALIDATED.  IF THE DATE IS
004100*        INVALID, A RETURN CODE OF 1 WILL BE RETURNED, AND THE
004200*        MESSAGE (I.E. The field must be a valid date...) WILL
004300*        WILL BE RETURNED.  IF THE DATE IS VALID, IT WILL BE
004400*        CONVERTED INTO VARIOUS FORMATS OF THE CORRECT STYLE.
      *        THEN USE ANY OF THESE CONVERTED DATES THAT YOU NEED.
004600*
004700*        MODE 4 IS USED TO TAKE A DATE FROM THE DATABASE AND
      *        TRANSFORM IT INTO FORMATS READABLE BY THE USER.
004900*        SIMPLY PASS A DATABASE DATE IN YYMMDD FORMAT, AND IT
005000*        WILL BE RETURNED IN USER FORMATS OF THE CORRECT STYLE.
005100*
005200*    THE PARAMETERS HAVE THE FOLLOWING MEANINGS:
005300*
005400*    DATE-CODE     -  CAN BE EITHER 1, 3, OR 0.
005500*
005600*      1  DATE STYLE IS AMERICAN (MMDDYY)
005700*
005800*      3  DATE STYLE IS EUROPEAN (DDMMYY)
005900*
006000*      0  NO DATE CODE IS PASSED.  IN THIS CASE THE SUBPROGRAM
006100*         WILL DETERMINE THE DATE CODE FROM THE FILE "DDATECOD",
006200*         AND RETURN IT TO THE CALLING PROGRAM. IN THIS CASE ON
      *         THE SECOND AND ALL FOLLOWING CALLS TO THE SUBPROGRAM,
      *         THE DATE CODE WILL NOT HAVE TO BE DETERMINED.
006500*         IF THE FILE "DDATECOD" DOES NOT EXIST, THE DEFAULT CODE
006600*         WILL BE 1.
006700*
006800*    THE SUBPROGRAM CAN BE CALLED IN VARIOUS MODES, AS
006900*    FOLLOWS:
007000*
007100*    0  EITHER SYSTEM DATE OR DISPLAY DATE IS PASSED IN X(6) FORMAT
      *       EITHER DISPLAY DATE OR DATABASE DATE IS RETURNED IN X(6)
      *       AND ONE OF THE FOLLOWING NUMBERS IS ADDED TO "DATE-CODE"
      *       TO SPECIFY:
      *         0  SYSTEM DATE PASSED, DISPLAY DATE RETURNED
      *            -  SYSTEM DATE PASSED MMDDYY
      *            -  DISPLAY DATE RETURNED MMDDYY IF AMERICAN
      *            -  DISPLAY DATE RETURNED DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN
      *
      *         3  DISPLAY DATE PASSED, DATABASE DATE RETURNED
      *            -  DISPLAY DATE PASSED MMDDYY IF AMERICAN
      *            -  DISPLAY DATE PASSED DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN
      *            -  DATABASE DATE RETURNED MMDDYY
      *
008500*        6  SYSTEM DATE PASSED, DATABASE DATE RETURNED
008600*           -  SYSTEM DATE PASSED MMDDYY
008700*           -  DATABASE DATE RETURNED MMDDYY
008800*
008900*    1  NO DATE IS PASSED
009000*       a. FORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-SLASH-OUT"
009100*            -  MM/DD/YY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
009200*            -  DD/MM/YY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
009300*       b. UNFORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-OUT"
009400*            -  MMDDYY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
009500*            -  DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
009600*       c. DATABASE DATE IS RETURNED AS YYMMDD IN "DATE-YMD-OUT".
009700*       d. FORMATTED TIME IS RETURNED IN "FORMATTED-TIME-OUT"
009800*            -  HH:MN:SS FORMAT
009900*       e. UNFORMATTED TIME IS RETURNED IN "UNFORMATTED-TIME-OUT"
010000*            -  HHMNSS FORMAT
010100*
010200*    2  SYSTEM DATE IS PASSED (MM/DD/YY) IN "DATE-VALIDATE-IN"
010300*       a. FORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-SLASH-OUT"
010400*            -  MM/DD/YY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
010500*            -  DD/MM/YY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
010600*       b. UNFORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-OUT"
010700*            -  MMDDYY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
010800*            -  DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
010900*       c. DATABASE DATE IS RETURNED AS YYMMDD IN "DATE-YMD-OUT".
011000*
011100*    3  DISPLAY DATE FROM SCREEN IS PASSED IN "DATE-VALIDATE-IN".
011200*         -  MONTH, DAY, YEAR IF AMERICAN STYLE
011300*         -  DAY, MONTH, YEAR IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
011400*         -  THE DATE CAN BE IN ANY FORMAT (I.E. FOR EUROPEAN,
011500*            5 JAN 85, 05 JANUARY 85, OR 050185 WOULD BE VALID).
011600*       a. FORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-SLASH-OUT"
011700*            -  MM/DD/YY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
011800*            -  DD/MM/YY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
011900*       b. UNFORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-OUT"
012000*            -  MMDDYY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
012100*            -  DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
012200*       c. DATABASE DATE IS RETURNED AS YYMMDD IN "DATE-YMD-OUT".
012300*       d. A 1 IS RETURNED IN "DATE-RET-CODE" IF THE DATE IS
012400*          INVALID.
012500*       e. AN ERROR MESSAGE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-MSG" IF THE DATE
012600*          IS INVALID.
012700*
012800*    4  DATABASE DATE IS PASSED AS YYMMDD IN "DATE-VALIDATE-IN"
012900*       a. FORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-SLASH-OUT"
013000*            -  MM/DD/YY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
013100*            -  DD/MM/YY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
013200*       b. UNFORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-OUT"
013300*            -  MMDDYY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
      *            -  DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
      *       C.  DATABASE DATE IS RETURNED AS YYMMDD IN "DATE-YMD-OUT"
013600*           (THIS DUPLICATES WHAT WAS INPUT IN "DATE-VALIDATE-IN").
013700*
013800**************************************************************
013900*    PROGRAM CHANGES:                                        *
014000*   09/19/85  ADDED CALLS TO FINDJCW, NLAPPEND, CATOPEN, AND *
014100*             CATCLOSE IN ORDER TO ACCOMODATE THE NATIVE     *
014200*             LANGUAGE SUPPORT FACILITY.  ADDED LINKAGES AND *
014300*             ALSO MADE THE CHANGE TO THE FORMFILE NAMES.    *
014400*                                     -T W COTTON            *
014500**************************************************************
014600*
014700*    03/04/86.
014800*        CHANGED THE WAY THIS SUBPROGRAM HANDLES THE SITUATION
014900*        IN MODE 3 (USER DATE) IF A DATE OF SPACES IS PASSED.
015000*        PREVIOUSLY, THE DATE WOULD BE FLAGGED AS INVALID.
015100*        NOW, WILL GIVE A GOOD RETURN CODE, BUT WILL RETURN
015200*        SPACES IN THE VARIOUS DATE FIELDS.  THIS IS TO AVOID
015300*        THE FOLLOWING TYPE OF LOGIC IN THE CALLING PROGRAMS:
015400*          IF DATA-ENTRY-DATE = SPACES
015500*              MOVE SPACES         TO  DATABASE-DATE
015600*          ELSE
015700*              MOVE DATA-ENTRY-DATE TO DATE-VALIDATE-IN
015800*              CALL "TDATECHK"............
015900*        CIH.
016000*
016100*    03/07/86
016200*      CHANGED PROGRAM FOR MODE 4 - IF THE DATABASE DATE
016300*      IS SPACES, RETURNS SPACES IN "DATE-SLASH-OUT"
016400*      INSTEAD OF "  /  /  ".  CIH.
016500*
      *  ****** N O T E ! *******  THE CATREAD AND FOPEN OF DATE
      *  FILE FUNCTIONS ARE YET TO BE IMPLEMENTED IN HERE!
      *
      *    11/23/93      BK DISMUKES
      *      ADDED LOGIC TO RECOGNIZE EUROPEAN DATE FORMAT.
      *
016600 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
016700 CONFIGURATION SECTION.
016800 SOURCE-COMPUTER. HP-3000.
016900 OBJECT-COMPUTER. HP-3000.
017000*SPECIAL-NAMES.
017100*    CONDITION-CODE IS C-C.
017200 DATA DIVISION.
017300 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       COPY CATREAD IN COPYLIB.
017400 01  SAVE-AREA                     PIC X(2).
017500 01  DATE-WORK.
017600     05  DATE-WORK-MD              PIC 9(2).
017700     05  DATE-WORK-DM              PIC 9(2).
017800     05  DATE-WORK-YY              PIC 9(2).
017900 01  LEAP-YEAR-FLAG                PIC X(1)  VALUE "N".
018000 01  LEAP-TEST                     PIC 9(4)V9(4).
018100 01  LEAP-REDEF REDEFINES LEAP-TEST.
018200     05  FILLER                    PIC 9(4).
018300     05  LEAP-TEST-DEC             PIC 9(4).
018400
       01  IBM-DATE-WORK.
           05  IBM-DATE-WORK-YY          PIC X(2).
           05  IBM-DATE-WORK-MM          PIC X(2).
           05  IBM-DATE-WORK-DD          PIC X(2).
018500
018600 01  DDATECOD-FILE  PIC X(22) VALUE "DDATECOD/DONTPURG.PUB".
018700 01  DDATECOD-FNUM  PIC S9(4) COMP-4 VALUE 0.
018800
018300 COPY  CCHKOBJ    IN  COPYLIB.
018300
018900 LINKAGE SECTION.
019000 01  DATE-CHECK-AREA.
019100     05  DATE-CODE                 PIC S9(4) COMP-4.
019200     05  DATE-MODE                 PIC S9(4) COMP-4.
019300     05  DATE-IN.
019400         10  DATE-IN-MD            PIC X(2).
019500         10  DATE-IN-DM            PIC X(2).
019600         10  DATE-IN-YY            PIC X(2).
019700     05  DATE-OUT.
019800         10  DATE-OUT-MD           PIC X(2).
019900         10  DATE-OUT-DM           PIC X(2).
020000         10  DATE-OUT-YY           PIC X(2).
020100     05  DATE-RET-CODE             PIC S9(4) COMP-4.
020200     05  DATE-VALIDATE-IN          PIC X(20).
020300*----- DATE TYPE EXAMPLES
020400*----- DATE-TYPE-0             030585
020500*----- DATE-TYPE-1             03/05/85
020600*----- DATE-TYPE-2             03/5/85
020700*----- DATE-TYPE-3             3/05/85
020800*----- DATE-TYPE-4             3/5/85
020900     05  DATE-TYPE-0 REDEFINES DATE-VALIDATE-IN.
021000         10  DATE-NUMERIC          PIC X(6).
021100         10  FILLER                PIC X(14).
021200     05  DATE-TYPE-1 REDEFINES DATE-VALIDATE-IN.
021300         10  DT1-MD                PIC X(2).
021400         10  DT1-S1                PIC X(1).
021500         10  DT1-DM                PIC X(2).
021600         10  DT1-S2                PIC X(1).
021700         10  DT1-YY                PIC X(2).
021800         10  FILLER                PIC X(12).
021900     05  DATE-TYPE-2 REDEFINES DATE-VALIDATE-IN.
022000         10  DT2-MD                PIC X(2).
022100         10  DT2-S1                PIC X(1).
022200         10  DT2-DM                PIC X(1).
022300         10  DT2-S2                PIC X(1).
022400         10  DT2-YY                PIC X(2).
022500         10  FILLER                PIC X(13).
022600     05  DATE-TYPE-3 REDEFINES DATE-VALIDATE-IN.
022700         10  DT3-MD                PIC X(1).
022800         10  DT3-S1                PIC X(1).
022900         10  DT3-DM                PIC X(2).
023000         10  DT3-S2                PIC X(1).
023100         10  DT3-YY                PIC X(2).
023200         10  FILLER                PIC X(13).
023300     05  DATE-TYPE-4 REDEFINES DATE-VALIDATE-IN.
023400         10  DT4-MD                PIC X(1).
023500         10  DT4-S1                PIC X(1).
023600         10  DT4-DM                PIC X(1).
023700         10  DT4-S2                PIC X(1).
023800         10  DT4-YY                PIC X(2).
023900         10  FILLER                PIC X(14).
024000     05  DATE-YMD-OUT.
024100         10  DATE-YMD-OUT-YY       PIC X(2).
024200         10  DATE-YMD-OUT-MM       PIC X(2).
024300         10  DATE-YMD-OUT-DD       PIC X(2).
024400     05  DATE-SLASH-OUT.
024500         10  DATE-SLASH-OUT-MD     PIC X(2).
024600         10  DATE-SLASH-OUT-S1     PIC X(1).
024700         10  DATE-SLASH-OUT-DM     PIC X(2).
024800         10  DATE-SLASH-OUT-S2     PIC X(1).
024900         10  DATE-SLASH-OUT-YY     PIC X(2).
025000     05  FORMATTED-TIME-OUT.
025100         10  FORMATTED-TIME-HH     PIC X(2).
025200         10  FORMATTED-TIME-C1     PIC X(1).
025300         10  FORMATTED-TIME-MN     PIC X(2).
025400         10  FORMATTED-TIME-C2     PIC X(1).
025500         10  FORMATTED-TIME-SS     PIC X(2).
025600     05  UNFORMATTED-TIME-OUT.
